 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Function",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "A and B feed an OR stage whose result is ANDed with C. C low forces Y low; with C high, Y is high if A or B is high and low if both are low."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Three configurations",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Fixing one input at a rail gives a simpler gate: C at VCC makes a 2-input OR of A and B; A at GND makes a 2-input AND of B and C; B at GND makes a 2-input AND of A and C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input hysteresis",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The inputs have hysteresis, typically 250 mV at 3.3 V, which tolerates slow input edges and improves noise immunity at the inputs."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Inputs above VCC",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Inputs may be driven up to 5.5 V whatever the supply, within the recommended 0 V to 5.5 V input range."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Partial power-down",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Ioff circuitry turns the output off while the part is unpowered, so current cannot flow back through it into a VCC rail that is down. Ioff is specified with VCC = 0 and 5.5 V on an input or the output."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Unused inputs",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "No input may float: tie every unused input to VCC or GND."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Operating life",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "The silicon's operating-life design goal is 10 years at a 105 °C junction temperature, excluding package interconnect life. Estimated life falls as junction temperature rises: about 60 years at 85 °C and about 2.3 years at 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Enhanced product",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The -EP version is made under a controlled baseline at a single fabrication site and a single assembly and test site, with an extended product life cycle, extended notice of product changes and product traceability. It is rated for the military range, -55 °C to 125 °C; other temperature ranges can be made to order. It has catalog (SN74LVC1G3208) and automotive (SN74LVC1G3208-Q1) counterparts."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Timing measurement",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "Propagation delay is measured from the input crossing VM to the output crossing VM, with VM at VCC/2 (1.5 V at 3.3 V). CL counts the probe and fixture capacitance. The 15 pF table uses the 1 MΩ load, the 30 pF or 50 pF tables the 1 kΩ or 500 Ω load."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package and mounting",
   "page": 13,
   "text": "Body dimensions exclude mold flash and protrusions, which add at most 0.25 mm per side. Leads 1 to 3 may be wider than leads 4 to 6 to show orientation. The outline follows JEDEC MO-178."
  }
 ],
